            <ArticleTitle>Grading of pain and anxiety. Comparison between a linear analogue and a computerised audiovisual analogue scale.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>875-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Comparison of a linear analogue scale on paper and a computerised audiovisual analogue scale presented on a visual display unit is described. Pain was assessed postoperatively in 109 patients and anxiety pre-operatively in 146 patients. Results show a strong correlation between gradings obtained using the two methods, indicating the computerised method is as reliable as the conventional one.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
